        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Identify the foci of the hyperbola. Given \\( F_1 = (10, 2) \\) and \\( F_2 = (-16, 2) \\), the center of the hyperbola is the midpoint of the segment joining the foci. Thus, the center \\( (h, k) \\) is calculated as follows:\n\\[ h = \\frac{10 + (-16)}{2} = \\frac{-6}{2} = -3 \\]\n\\[ k = \\frac{2 + 2}{2} = 2 \\]\nSo, the center of the hyperbola is \\( (-3, 2) \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 559,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 561,
        "char_start": 361,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 231,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 232,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Determine the distance between the foci, which is \\( 2c \\). The distance between \\( F_1 \\) and \\( F_2 \\) is:\n\\[ 2c = \\sqrt{(10 - (-16))^2 + (2 - 2)^2} = \\sqrt{26^2} = 26 \\]\nThus, \\( c = 13 \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 793,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 795,
        "char_start": 563,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 317,
